ed","position":{"commit_sha":"8b721af90defd874f113a4bcd63d060169f47fa1","position":"1788159549372954668-75fee403-c5c9-4981-8a80-8142cf9022ed"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f08ca1031e86513b6f8ae2ed5d9cae4b2e6910616a85415a5aedd427bcfaf8c1","event_uuid":"445dfd9a-bd3e-4435-94c9-058738e0b13c","position":{"commit_sha":"082e6ec4f41a2f08ad0b733f863ac78ab189acbe","position":"1788160558755909001-445dfd9a-bd3e-4435-94c9-058738e0b13c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bcce7ffbf70fe8a2587a9906ba2a03cfb228815b0f042af09d4ebc46f9211430","event_uuid":"65f6933c-cadd-4d6a-b169-5514c14e8d20","position":{"commit_sha":"80c4e6c71057f6c5b3a5393060f2f6aff9089f9f","position":"1788161019966316692-65f6933c-cadd-4d6a-b169-5514c14e8d20"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788112435373314417,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f379a6e5-22ef-477c-aaad-deb1d0fb5ebc","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fc84-a6a6-14c3-4bc8"},{"link_uuid":"cba1753d-6efa-45a0-8482-fa7c7f806b14","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7dbd-de27-73d3-4065"},{"link_uuid":"bb34f246-ee76-4d4c-9ef1-9fb20f7590cd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0738-4150-40bb-4c06"}],"description":"## Problem\nOnce the review-kernel's downstream consumers no longer read `severity` (sibling tickets 1-5),\nthe review-kernel (`pass3_decide`) itself should stop STAMPING `severity` onto its own emitted\nfindings. `pass3_decide` has FIVE return sites that stamp `severity`\n(`review_kernel/decide.py`): four via a `sev = severity_label(imp)` variable (lines 690, 706,\n724, 740) and one hardcoded literal `\"none\"` on the no-verification/indeterminate return\n(line 673, which occurs before `imp`/`sev` are ever computed).\n\nCRITICAL MECHANISM (found by plan-review): omitting `severity` at the source is NOT enough by\nitself. `code_review/shim.py::_to_common_finding` currently ALWAYS stamps a valid `severity`\nvia `_KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY.get(raw_sev, _SEVERITY_DEFAULT)` -- for a kernel finding with\nno `severity` at all, `raw_sev` is `\"\"`, which the map doesn't recognize, so it falls back to\n`_SEVERITY_DEFAULT = \"medium\"`. And even if `_to_common_finding` is fixed to omit the key\nentirely, the finding still flows through `finalize_findings` -> `build_result` ->\n`findings.py::normalize_finding`, which TODAY unconditionally re-stamps a missing `severity`\nto `\"info\"` (`f[\"severity\"] = sev if sev in SEVERITIES else \"info\"`, where an absent key\ndefaults to `\"\"`, which isn't in `SEVERITIES`). So a naive \"just omit it in shim.py\" plan would\nship review-kernel findings that always carry `severity: \"medium\"` or `severity: \"info\"`\nregardless -- silently reintroducing a meaningless label, exactly the problem this epic\nretires. `normalize_finding` must be changed too: only clamp to `\"info\"` when a `severity` key\nIS PRESENT but holds an unrecognized value; leave it ABSENT when the input genuinely has no\n`severity` key. Research confirmed this is safe: no production caller or existing test relies\non `normalize_finding` backfilling `\"info\"` onto a finding dict that never had a `severity`\nkey at all (every other real producer -- `completion_reconcile.py`, `completion_child_gate.py`,\n`workflow/gate_ops.py`, `spec_scan.py` -- always supplies a real severity value already).\n\nCORRECTED SCOPE (post-decomposition research): `findings.py`'s shared `SEVERITIES` vocabulary\nand the `Finding` Pydantic field are NOT removed -- they serve the completion-verification\nmodule cluster and `spec_scan.py`, neither of which has a priority/decision alternative.\n`completion_verdict.schema.json` and `review_result.schema.json` both `$ref` the SAME shared\n`common.schema.json#/$defs/finding` (confirmed, byte-identical `$ref`), so relaxing that def's\n`required` list technically loosens both schemas' formal requirement -- but every\ncompletion-verification producer always populates `severity` in practice regardless of the\nschema requirement, so this is a de jure relaxation only, with no de facto behavior change for\n`completion_verdict`.\n\n## Approach\n1. In `review_kernel/decide.py`, remove `severity`/`sev` from ALL FIVE `pass3_decide` return\n   sites: the four `sev`-fed sites (lines 690, 706, 724, 740) AND the hardcoded `\"none\"`\n   literal on the no-verification return (line 673). Keep `severity_label()` itself as an\n   internal impact-bucketing helper (still used by calibration/eval code and\n   `test_divergence_grade_split.py`), just stop writing its output into the finding.\n2. In `code_review/shim.py::_to_common_finding`, stop defaulting an absent/unrecognized\n   `severity` to `_SEVERITY_DEFAULT = \"medium\"` -- when the source kernel finding has no\n   `severity` key (now the normal case for review-kernel findings), omit the `severity` key\n   from the output entirely. Delete `_KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY` and `_SEVERITY_DEFAULT` from\n   `shim.py` (their only use site).\n3. In `findings.py::normalize_finding`, change the severity-clamp so it only fires when a\n   `severity` key IS PRESENT on the input but holds a value outside `SEVERITIES` (still clamps\n   to `\"info\"` in that case, unchanged); when the input has NO `severity` key at all, leave it\n   absent on the output rather than backfilling `\"info\"`.\n4. In `common.schema.json`'s `$defs/finding`, remove `severity` from the `required` list\n   (leave the `severity` property and the `$defs/severity` enum definition in place).\n5. Remove the vestigial `DEFAULT_BLOCKING_SEVERITIES`/`blocking_severities` field and its\n   env-var registration from `review_bot/config.py` (already unused in the current\n   `code_review_decision` flow per `adapter.py`'s own docstring).\n6. Add ONE compatibility-note entry to `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`: `severity`\n   is no longer guaranteed present on review-kernel-sourced findings within `review_result`\n   (the shared schema field is now optional, not removed); every other producer (including\n   `completion_verdict`'s) continues to always supply it in practice.\n7. Amend `docs/adr/0108-retire-severity-label.md` with an \"Amendment\" section recording this\n   corrected, narrower scope, including the `normalize_finding` fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `grep -n '\"severity\"' src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py` finds no finding-shape\n  stamping at ANY of the five return sites (the `severity_label` function definition and any\n  historical comments are acceptable).\n- [x] `findings.py::normalize_finding({\"finding\": \"x\", \"dimension\": \"d\", \"detail\": \"y\"})` (no\n  `severity` key at all) returns a dict with NO `severity` key; `normalize_finding({\"severity\":\n  \"BOGUS\", ...})` still returns `severity: \"info\"` (the existing invalid-value clamp is\n  unchanged) -- both asserted by strengthened/new tests in `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`.\n- [x] A new or strengthened test feeds a kernel finding with NO `severity` key through the full\n  production path (`shim.py::_verdict_to_review_result` -> `finalize_findings` ->\n  `normalize_finding`) and asserts the FINAL `review_result` finding has no `severity` key --\n  not just `_to_common_finding`'s intermediate output, so the `normalize_finding` re-stamp\n  path is actually covered.\n- [x] `common.schema.json`'s `$defs/finding.required` no longer lists `severity`; the\n  `severity` property and `$defs/severity` enum remain defined.\n- [x] `review_bot/config.py` has no `blocking_severities`/`DEFAULT_BLOCKING_SEVERITIES` symbol;\n  `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` and `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` are updated to\n  assert the symbol's absence.\n- [x] `grep -n \"_KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY\\|_SEVERITY_DEFAULT\" src/rebar/llm/code_review/shim.py`\n  returns no matches.\n- [x] `docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and `docs/adr/0108-retire-severity-label.md`\n  (Amendment section) each record the corrected, narrower scope.\n- [x] `make test` passes with the full suite, including\n  `pytest tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py -k test_severity_label_buckets` and\n  `pytest tests/unit/test_divergence_grade_split.py` (proving `severity_label()` itself is\n  untouched) and the full `completion_reconcile`/`completion_child_gate`/`epic_bug_screen`\n  test suites (proving the completion-verification cluster's own `severity` usage is\n  unaffected).\n\n## Testing\nTier: in-process unit tests. Oracle (three layers, since a single-layer test previously missed\nthe re-stamp defect): (1) `pass3_decide`'s real output has no `severity` key at any of its\nfive return paths; (2) `normalize_finding` in isolation -- absent-key input stays absent,\npresent-invalid-value input still clamps to `\"info\"`; (3) the FULL production chain\n(`shim.py` -> `finalize_findings` -> `normalize_finding`) fed a severity-less kernel finding\nproduces a `review_result` finding with no `severity` key -- proving the omission actually\nsurvives to the schema-validated output, not just an intermediate function's return value.\nContrast/negative case: a `completion_reconcile.py`-shaped finding (always carries `severity:\n\"high\"`) fed through the SAME `normalize_finding` continues to carry `severity` unchanged,\nproving the narrower scope holds.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py","reason":"stop stamping severity at all five pass3_decide return sites"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/shim.py","reason":"stop defaulting absent severity to medium, delete _KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY/_SEVERITY_DEFAULT"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/findings.py","reason":"normalize_finding only clamps when severity present-but-invalid, leaves absent-key inputs absent"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json","reason":"relax severity from required to optional on the shared finding def"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/config.py","reason":"remove vestigial BLOCKING_SEVERITIES/blocking_severities/_severities_env"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py","reason":"fix stale docstring comment referencing the removed blocking_severities field"},{"path":"scripts/gen_env_registry.py","reason":"remove the stale _severities_env row from the env-read helper registry"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated after removing the BLOCKING_SEVERITIES row"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"compatibility-note entry"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"compatibility-note entry"},{"path":"docs/adr/0108-retire-severity-label.md","reason":"Amendment section recording the corrected narrower scope"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"fix documented review_code() usage example that unconditionally read severity"},{"path":"docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md","reason":"remove stale BLOCKING_SEVERITIES operator-config documentation"},{"path":"docs/adr/0077-code-review-voter-four-pass-rewire.md","reason":"note blocking_severities removal completed the anticipated follow-on"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"update tests asserting BLOCKING_SEVERITIES absence"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","reason":"update test asserting BLOCKING_SEVERITIES absence"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py","reason":"test normalize_finding absent-stays-absent and pres